{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative","id":814634,"title":"What Exactly Prevents The True Fae From Being Creative?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-22T20:35:44-08:00","id":814634,"title":"What Exactly Prevents The True Fae From Being Creative?","content":"Is it their solipsistic perspective? An ancient Contract they broke? A simple lack of incentive/necessity?<br /> <br /> If a True Fae found a loophole in the Wyrd that is just big enough for them to gain a spark of creativity, does that True Fae run the risk of turning into a Charlatan as if connecting too deeply with a mortal?<br /> <br /> Another relevant question: if the Wyrd allowed a True Fae to have creativity, what would be the Catch?<br /> <br /> I'm asking partly because there is this faction from the SCP Foundation called <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/groups-of-interest#toc5\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Dr. Wondertainment</b></a>. I always thought that, if said company has a singular entity as its owner, it could very well be a True Fae with the capacity to create new things. Just read <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-438315/dr-wondertainment-and-his-whimsical-toys\" target=\"_blank\"><b>the thread where the users of the SCP Foundation wiki discuss their theories about Wondertainment</b></a>, and you'll see how I came to that conclusion.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to have something like that faction in the CoD, would the owner work better as a really powerful hobgoblin merchant?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yes, I realize that a big part of the appeal is not knowing who or what Wondertainment is, or how the toys are made. I am just focusing on a Changeling-centered possibility. I'm sure there many equally interesting alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-22-2016, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T21:50:10-08:00","id":814657,"title":"","content":"The Fae are borrowers, to put it charitably. They are director-performers, to put it kindly. They are, to dispense entirely with pretty poesies, lying stealing control-freaks who only exist insofar as they are <i>relevant</i>, and they cannot claim relevance amid the riotous march of ages without connections, because the desperate passion that drives them is antithetical to the prospect of making the One New Thing that will Put Them On The Map, and Faerie is by definition Off The Map.<br /> <br /> If a Fae has ever succeeded in legitimately making something new, it's probably been the culmination of Legend after Legend leading up to Transcendence. To have it be otherwise is to make the Gentry knowable, and the Strangers are definitionally Strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T22:25:46-08:00","id":814664,"title":"","content":"Confirming the nutshell-Because if a True Fae created something, they've Transcended their current state of being, from story-told to storytellers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T03:00:54-08:00","id":814743,"title":"","content":"I like understanding of True Fae as avatars ( or residents ) of Lower Depths realm that sustain itself on dreams and creativity of mortals. In the end, Gentry kidnaps changelings to hear ( and relive ) stories that mortals talk themselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T06:29:59-08:00","id":814809,"title":"","content":"Short answer is: lacking souls. Imagination, creative acts and free will are the prerrogative of those who have them. That\u00b4s the primary reason the Fae are so fascinated with humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:22:28-08:00","id":814996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=814664#post814664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Confirming the nutshell-Because if a True Fae created something, they've Transcended their current state of being, from story-told to storytellers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does all of them have a personal Story even if they're not engaged in a Legend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:25:01-08:00","id":814998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=814996#post814996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does all of them have a personal Story even if they're not engaged in a Legend?</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>are</i> their stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:26:31-08:00","id":814999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=814998#post814998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They <i>are</i> their stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Listen to Satchel. Satchel has this marvellous ability to spell out the metaphysics of any given series he looks at with astounding...well, clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:23:07-08:00","id":815031,"title":"","content":"The True Fae are not really people. That's the gist of it. They make really good mimicries, for sure, but they're more like an inhuman spirit or alien trying to pretend they're vaguely human by adopting an archetypical story-form. The True Fae are more like intelligent, self-aware stories than actual comprehensible entities.<br /> <br /> The personal horror that comes from changelings becoming True Fae is not &quot;oh no, I'm going to become an amoral tormentor!&quot;, but &quot;oh no, I'm going to <i>stop being human in any recognisable way!</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The point of this is that True Fae can't have creativity due to the same reasons that a storm or a book can't have creativity. They're not people and they don't have souls. If anything, you could wonder how much of the True Fae's actions are just self-sustaining motions they go through. They play they part and seek relevance because that's what passes for &quot;eating and breathing&quot; for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 01-23-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:21:06-08:00","id":815094,"title":"","content":"And now I've got this mental image of Lovecraftian fish-things eating Trope-flakes that fall into the ocean from passing humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:18:00-08:00","id":815122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=814999#post814999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listen to Satchel. Satchel has this marvellous ability to spell out the metaphysics of any given series he looks at with astounding...well, clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh speaking,of clarity,doesw the corebook talks about that if a changeling has a abnormally high wyrd and low clarity,they might become true fae themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:21:23-08:00","id":815124,"title":"","content":"The Becoming Nightmare mechanic is nowhere in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:29:38-08:00","id":815129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=815124#post815124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Becoming Nightmare mechanic is nowhere in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />,i really wanted to see more more of that,is not even talked about in the fluff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:40:09-08:00","id":815133,"title":"","content":"IIRC the first and possibly only time they talked about changelings becoming True Fae was in Equinox Road, originally supposed to be the last Lost book. I could be wrong though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:52:37-08:00","id":815140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=815133#post815133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC the first and possibly only time they talked about changelings becoming True Fae was in Equinox Road, originally supposed to be the last Lost book. I could be wrong though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's implied in multiple places as early as the 1e corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:53:23-08:00","id":815141,"title":"","content":"And it's implied in the 2E core. Just lacking mechanics. And confirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-23-2016, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:59:26-08:00","id":815146,"title":"","content":"Beast talks about it as well,that's why i asked if it was still present on the second edition<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In their rise to power and eventual Inheritance, Beasts<br /> highlight a common fear among changelings: that of becoming<br /> the very thing they hate and fear. Unlike a vampire\u2019s Golconda<br /> or a mage\u2019s Ascension, most changelings look on the prospect<br /> of apotheosis \u2014 of harnessing their Wyrd to become essentially<br /> True Fae themselves \u2014 as a fate worse than death. The fact that<br /> Beasts seem sanguine about becoming creatures of nightmarish<br /> predation makes them creatures to be feared. On the other<br /> hand, Beasts are some of the few beings the Gentry interact with<br /> on something like equal terms, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T21:27:49-08:00","id":815238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=814657#post814657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fae are borrowers, to put it charitably. They are director-performers, to put it kindly. They are, to dispense entirely with pretty poesies, lying stealing control-freaks who only exist insofar as they are <i>relevant</i>, and they cannot claim relevance amid the riotous march of ages without connections, because the desperate passion that drives them is antithetical to the prospect of making the One New Thing that will Put Them On The Map, and Faerie is by definition Off The Map.<br /> <br /> If a Fae has ever succeeded in legitimately making something new, it's probably been the culmination of Legend after Legend leading up to Transcendence. To have it be otherwise is to make the Gentry knowable, and the Strangers are definitionally Strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if they're supposed to be some kind of internal commentary about how there are no new ideas?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no such thing as a new idea. It is impossible. We simply take a lot of old ideas and put them into a sort of mental kaleidoscope. We give them a turn and they make new and curious combinations. We keep on turning and making new combinations indefinitely; but they are the same old pieces of colored glass that have been in use through all the ages. </div> </div> </div>- <i>Mark Twain, a Biography </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T21:39:44-08:00","id":815246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=815238#post815238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they're supposed to be some kind of internal commentary about how there are no new ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tall Blue Man can't go home because of precisely that dilemma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tell me a story.</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Arcadia, the Tall Blue Man could make the trees applaud and the rivers weep with his renditions of the classic stories. Of course, he never made up his own tales \u2014 the True Fae lack that capacity. But he could <u>re</u>tell them with such skill that the Gentry from all over the land would ask for their favorite tales, over and over, and the Tall Blue Man was happy to oblige.<br /> <br /> Pride was his undoing. He visited the manse of a Fae lord with a perfect memory, a lord who was so old that the stones didn\u2019t remember his childhood. He remembered every story he\u2019d ever heard, and after seven days of listening to the Tall Blue Man rattle off his repertoire, the Fae lord scoffed that he\u2019d heard all of these tales before, and that truly the Tall Blue Man could show him nothing new. And the Tall Blue Man responded with tales that he had heard from changelings, stories that originated from the world of mortals, and the lord answered that he had heard these, too. There <u>were</u> no new tales, he said bitterly. Everything \u201cnew\u201d was just an old story with some new dressing. The bard told the lord that he would travel as far as was necessary to find a new tale, and would not return until he did.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T02:01:38-08:00","id":815962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=814999#post814999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listen to Satchel. Satchel has this marvellous ability to spell out the metaphysics of any given series he looks at with astounding...well, clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the best things about Satchel is his ability to consistently do this. He's either been reading the minds of writers or he's been tying roleplaying games to operating tables and <i>vivisecting </i>them in his spare time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T23:05:19-08:00","id":819705,"title":"","content":"I recently had an idea for a story, inspired by events in my own life, and it suddenly hit me why the True Fae can only imitate and copy: they have no life experience. Even the most fantastical of human stories is built on a foundation of lived experience. We may not have ever imagined a band of dwarves being attacked by giant spiders in a place called Mirkwood, but we are familiar with spiders, and we've been to a forest (or at least some place that had some trees), and we've been told that dwarves look like little bearded men, an idea not so far from our own daily life.<br /> <br /> But none of the Fair Folk were ever bitten by a spider as a child, or got a dew-spangled web stuck in their hair. No fairy ever tried to climb a tree, only to fall hard on damp grass strewn with autumn leaves, or watched their father trim or shave his beard. As far as I understand it, Arcadia is ultimately mutable, and doesn't have any forests or spiders or beards, except when the Fae will them into being.<br /> <br /> This means that everything the True Fae create is based, at best, on the second-hand impressions of someone who has actually lived in a world with trees and clouds and houses and fathers. One of the Fae may ask a human captive, or perhaps a hobgoblin or other hedge-being that is familiar with the world, to describe trees to it. The subject of this interrogation might tell the Fairy everything they know about all the sorts of trees they can think of off the top of their heads, about oaks and pines and maples and willows. The Fae may then go on to make oaks out of glass (having previously learned some things about the substance) and create chimerical trees blending what it finds to be the most pleasing characteristics of the maple and the pine. Yet it would never occur to it to create any sort of fruit tree, or a stand of tropical hardwoods, for the simple reason that its sole informant on the nature of trees neglected to mention them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-30-2016, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T20:42:08-08:00","id":820711,"title":"","content":"One thing that has sort of stuck with me is that the True Fae are beings of quasi-infinite power in their own realms, practically gods and able to shape everything to their whims. Characters are given direction and inspiration by the limitations they have in their surroundings and lives. How exactly can you be creative when you have nothing that you have to struggle against? Anything that struggles directly against you can just be broken, and anything that tries to flee can just be followed, and even if they manage to destroy a part of you that's not the only part of you. You're ageless, they'll die even if you don't ignore them.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it in another way, it's like when you can do absolutely anything you could possibly want to and no idea on <i>what</i> to do. No guidelines means that you're able to do what you like, but by that same virtue you have nothing to form a basis from. Nothing to push against, confront, challenge or even conform to. You just end up copying things that you remember, other stories you liked and you just reuse them for your own purposes with the available materials (even if those materials sometimes rebel).<br /> <br /> Now, naturally not everyone has that issue - some people can't work with restrictions while others can't work well in a void (I'm one of them). I simply see the Gentry as those who, by virtue of having everything at their fingertips, can't figure out how to make anything new, just similar to what they know of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:59:26-08:00","id":822517,"title":"","content":"Huge thanks to everyone who took the time to make things clearer for me. If I ever use Dr. Wondertainment in a CoD, I'll do my best to stick closer to the original concept. My hunch is to interpret it as one of those corporations that turn people into Deviants. If I need to make it more nebulous, I'd make a Mystery (i.e. the stuff Mages investigate). A sort of metaphysical force that can take on the trappings of other phenomena associated with wondrous inventions (e.g. Infrastructure and Goblin Markets), but isn't really any of them. Perhaps the source of it all is a Rank 6 or 7 Alien (M:tAw - Summoners Chapter Four).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T20:34:23-08:00","id":827289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=815962#post815962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the best things about Satchel is his ability to consistently do this. He's either been reading the minds of writers or he's been tying roleplaying games to operating tables and <i>vivisecting </i>them in his spare time.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a True Fae who delights in pulling people into his twisted &quot;roleplaying games,&quot; carefully selecting his quarry from a web forum devoted to some horror game from the 90's, luring them with impossibly clear explanations of the game's setting that he uses to subtly weave his sick, horrific narrative into their lives.<br /> <br /> So the next time you thing you hear a clattering, like dice rolling out of sight?<br /> <br /> <i>Run.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:15:16-08:00","id":828003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative#post814634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it their solipsistic perspective? An ancient Contract they broke? A simple lack of incentive/necessity?<br /> <br /> If a True Fae found a loophole in the Wyrd that is just big enough for them to gain a spark of creativity, does that True Fae run the risk of turning into a Charlatan as if connecting too deeply with a mortal?<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I imagine that a True Fae with creativity is like a fictional character breaking the fourth wall. They realize they're in a narrative when nobody else seems to and by extension come across as being insane around the rest of the cast.<br /> <br /> From what I understand about True Fae, they thrive on narratives and roles. They kidnap people to help them act out the story, and when that changeling runs away, it throws the story out of whack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:18:54-08:00","id":828006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=815122#post815122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh speaking,of clarity,doesw the corebook talks about that if a changeling has a abnormally high wyrd and low clarity,they might become true fae themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Apparently if a Changeling has Wyrd 10, Clarity 0 and goes back to Arcadia, they become True Fae. Not sure if that's still how it works anymore or not with the second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T14:46:48-08:00","id":828441,"title":"","content":"That was an optional rule. It was always an optional rule.<br /> <br /> Second Edition picks up in the grand tradition of occasionally dropping the threat that changelings can become Strangers, but the actual Becoming Nightmare mechanic is nowhere in there. Because it's optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-11-2016, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T14:56:59-08:00","id":828446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=828441#post828441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was an optional rule. It was always an optional rule.<br /> <br /> Second Edition picks up in the grand tradition of occasionally dropping the threat that changelings can become Strangers, but the actual Becoming Nightmare mechanic is nowhere in there. Because it's optional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also it was never just &quot;max Wyrd, vent all Clarity, set foot in Faerie.&quot; There's <i>fate shenanigans</i> that factored into it as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T17:43:11-08:00","id":829045,"title":"","content":"You know something I always found weird? True Fae in 1ED had a limit of 1 dot for Expression, Empathy and Computers while in the mortal realm, and a limit of 3 dots elsewhere. Why wasn't there a limit for Crafts? And if the sterile imagination is a part of them, why would the limit change when they go to another dimension? I can understand if a Gentry uses a Hedgespun Raiment with a bonus for Expression, a Token violin and activates the 2nd clause of Vainglory, but why would the simple act of leaving the mortal realm affect the limit?<br /> <br /> If I really wanted to emphasize their lack of compassion and creativity, I'd put a limit of one dot for Expression, Empathy, Computers and Crafts, no matter where they are. And they can't have Specialties in those Skills either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T17:46:08-08:00","id":829047,"title":"","content":"Because Crafts is also used to repair objects. It's not just a creative skill. A mechanic, handyman, electrician, carpenter, plumber, etc., they all use a lot of Crafts but aren't exactly creative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T20:17:45-08:00","id":829086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814634-what-exactly-prevents-the-true-fae-from-being-creative?p=829045#post829045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the sterile imagination is a part of them, why would the limit change when they go to another dimension?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're natives of the place where the power of t